{"obsah":"<p>Another weekend in full swing. On Friday we were busy at the Mělník festival in Podolí park, which moved from the Mělník riverside. Two shows with 5 riders in a pleasant park setting were great. We also tested our new obstacle setup a bit more and new dual headset microphones for bigger events where we need two hosts. The spectators came to enjoy the event, so we could stretch out every show. Our obstacles were then used by the parkour athletes too. Martin Šimůnek once again proved that choosing volunteers is his weak point, when for the sideways jump he picked a local athlete who drew with Vlasta in the first show and blew him out like a candle in the athlete-vs-bike duel in the second.</p>\n\n<p>On Saturday we went to the Military Forests Days in Ralsko, which was a trial by fire … or rather by water, for Vlasta, Michal Budský and Nikol Kabeláčová. Rain, a flat tyre on the trailer, more rain and luckily a roughly 20-minute window for the exhibition right at the end of the event. The guys at the Javornice festival had a longer drive, but Lukáš Valný, Ondra Nenadál and Tobík Dolák enjoyed the beautiful weather and the event and showed the locals how to jump over obstacles. Martin Šimůnek also spent his Saturday elsewhere near Ústí, going wild at a corporate event. </p>\n\n<p>Photos for now are whatever we had, and hopefully something will arrive from the organisers, whom we thank for the invitation.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F06%2F355013175_648015220711209_1108277750721316203_n.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F06%2F355013175_648015220711209_1108277750721316203_n.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-237572\"/></a></figure